      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The summer has already redrawn Toronto's map - and it starts in the front office, where <strong>Dan Palango was hired as director of amateur scouting</strong>, with Rossen and Perpich joining the scouting staff too. That is not housekeeping; that is a signal. The Maple Leafs, who finished <strong>8th in the Atlantic Division with 78 points</strong>, are building for the next turn of the wheel, not polishing the last one. Their biggest swing remains Gavin McKenna, the No. 1 pick, a teenager with the kind of sheen that changes a room and forces a plan. Now the question is fit: who stays, who gets squeezed, and how much cap room can be turned into help before camp opens. <strong>The next item to watch is whether this new scouting group can convert July into October leverage.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 30, 2026"
      },
