        "body": "The reset is underway, and Toronto is making the summer look like a blueprint session. <strong>The Raptors have locked in their 2026 training camp in Quebec City and will stage a preseason game in Vancouver</strong>, a neat bit of geography that tells you this franchise wants to sell the next chapter before it has even finished assembling it. The roster math still matters more than the scenery: Toronto finished 3rd in the Atlantic Division, and the front office has to turn that old standing into a cleaner, taller, more coherent group. The Curry chatter has given the market a headline, but the real story is whether the Raptors can keep adding seasoned help without blocking their young core. <strong>What happens next in free agency will say whether this is a real push or just a fancy camp itinerary</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 30, 2026"
